 "note": "Verifier unanimity = all verifier labels identical; under ANLI's protocol (a 3rd verifier is added only when the first 2 disagree) this equals 'the first two verifiers agreed, no third needed', i.e. a k=2 line. k2_split counts any 2-label line whose two verifiers in fact disagree (expected 0). match/differ/no_majority partition each class's examples by whether the writer's gold equals / differs from / lacks a strict verifier majority. P1 (structural) bets ANLI's adversarial gold equals the verifier majority on more than 95% of examples in EVERY class. P2 (directional, a finding either way) bets neutral is the LEAST unanimously verified class, mirroring SNLI/MultiNLI. P3 bets the per-class unanimous-rate spread exceeds 0.05. Rates are reported, not pre-bet on guessed numbers. per_class is over all joined examples with a recognised gold; per_class_devtest and per_class_train split it (audit 39 showed the released verifier file also covers train). This audit measures AGREEMENT per class, not label correctness."
}